# Example production environment values — not secret. VITE_API_BASE_URL
# is safe to commit/see in browser dev tools either way, since Vite
# ships it to the client in the built JS regardless of where it comes
# from. This file documents the value; the GitHub Actions deploy
# workflow (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) is what actually sets it for
# the real production build — see VERSION_2_INTEGRATION_NOTES.md.
#
# Not auto-loaded by Vite (Vite only auto-loads .env/.env.local/
# .env.production, not .env.production.example) — this file is
# reference/documentation only. To build locally against the live
# Render backend instead of your local one, copy this to
# .env.production and run `npm run build -- --mode production`, or
# simply export VITE_API_BASE_URL before building.
#
# Version 7, Milestone 133: same-site API subdomain, not the
# onrender.com origin — see DOMAIN_CONNECTION_PLAN_CO_ZA.md. The old
# onrender.com URL still works during the transition; this is only the
# value the production frontend build itself should use.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.seasonedzgroup.co.za/api

# Milestone 183: Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID (e.g. "G-XXXXXXXXXX")
# — not secret (visible in every visitor's page source either way), but
# NOT hardcoded in .github/workflows/deploy.yml the way VITE_API_BASE_URL
# above is, since this one is owner-supplied and doesn't exist until a
# real GA4 property is created. The real production build reads it from
# the GitHub Actions repository VARIABLE named VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID
# (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> Variables tab on the
# repo, NOT a Secret), not from this file. To get a Measurement ID:
# create (or sign in to) a Google Analytics account at
# https://analytics.google.com, create a GA4 property for
# seasonedzgroup.co.za, add a Web data stream for
# https://www.seasonedzgroup.co.za, and copy the "Measurement ID" it
# shows (starts with "G-"). Until that repository variable is set,
# js/analytics.js keeps GA4 fully disabled in production — never a
# fabricated ID.
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
